{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And YHWH Elohim said to the serpent, etc.</b> Three things his speech caused: first, that it caused the removal of the light of His glory, may He be blessed, that hovered over Adam and his wife, as we wrote above — and this is the sod of the garments of light. Second, it caused Adam and Chavah to be cut off from this world, so that they would not live forever, as the punishment written in the verse states (Genesis 2:17): ״כִּי בְּיוֹם אֲכָלְךָ מִמֶּנּוּ מוֹת תָּמוּת״. Third, it caused that even during the days that they live in the world they would not enjoy the delights of Eden of Elohim, as stated (Genesis 3:24): ״וַיְגָרֶשׁ אֶת הָאָדָם״." "Corresponding to all three, he was punished with three: corresponding to the removal of the cloud of glory, which is the aspect of blessing, HaShem said to him ״אָרוּר״ etc. Corresponding to the cutting off of Adam from this world, his legs were cut off (Genesis Rabbah 20:10), for they correspond to man — the aspect of the absence of this world, which is the legs of the world of Asiyah. For you must know that if Adam had not eaten from the Tree of Knowledge, he would have existed in this world and in the supernal world as one, like a person dwelling in a house and in an upper chamber. And when he sinned he became physicalized and could no longer dwell in both together, but only in this world on its own; and when he wishes to ascend to the upper chamber, a transformation of the physical body is required, and this is the death of man. Therefore the serpent's legs were cut off. And corresponding to what he caused — to deprive Adam and Chavah of the enjoyment of the Garden of Eden — He said to him ״וְעָפָר תֹּאכַל״ etc., and they said, their memory for blessing (Yoma 75a), that whatever he eats he will taste nothing but the taste of dust. And accordingly it is precisely understood why HaShem said to the serpent at the beginning of His words ״כִּי עָשִׂיתָ זֹּאת״ — meaning, that the curses with which HaShem cursed him are his own deeds that he did, and they are our very words themselves. Understand this:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:51.396968122Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}